$DIR/main.p:15:14: invalid argument: mk() (value of type ring[int, 2]) for built-in len: len calls its Len method, which has a pointer receiver, so the operand must be addressable or a pointer
    len takes a string, an array or a pointer to one, a slice, a map, a channel,
    an owned, shared or synced array, or a value whose type has a method Len()
    int, such as a library container or a ring; len(E) of an enum type E is its
    number of members. A Len method with a pointer receiver needs an operand
    that is addressable or a pointer, as a method call would.
    Pass a value of one of these types, or store the value in a variable first.
    (see "Length and capacity" in the Plutonium spec, section 13.6)
    (run "pluto explain E0090" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/main.p:16:14: invalid argument: r (variable of type ring[int, 4]) for built-in cap: cap does not call methods; call its Cap method
    cap takes an array or a pointer to one, a slice or a channel. Unlike len, it
    does not call methods: a library container or a ring reports its capacity
    with a method of its own.
    Call the type's Cap method instead.
    (see "Length and capacity" in the Plutonium spec, section 13.6)
    (run "pluto explain E0084" for a longer explanation)
